<article class="env-lemma" id="02JR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02JR">Lemma <span data-tag="02JR">29.13.6</span>.</a> A quasi-compact immersion is quasi-affine. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $X \to S$ be a quasi-compact immersion. We have to show the inverse image of every affine open is quasi-affine. Hence, assuming $S$ is an affine scheme, we have to show $X$ is quasi-affine. By Lemma <a href="/tag/01RG" data-tag="01RG">29.7.7</a> the morphism $X \to S$ factors as $X \to Z \to S$ where $Z$ is a closed subscheme of $S$ and $X \subset Z$ is a quasi-compact open. Since $S$ is affine Lemma <a href="/tag/01QO" data-tag="01QO">29.2.1</a> implies $Z$ is affine. Hence we win. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>